When writing Tailwind v4 classes, always use named scale tokens instead of
arbitrary values when a matching token exists.

Examples:
  rounded-md        NOT rounded-[6px]
  rounded-lg        NOT rounded-[8px]
  rounded-xl        NOT rounded-[12px]
  text-sm           NOT text-[12px]
  text-xs           NOT text-[11px]
  p-4               NOT p-[16px]
  gap-1             NOT gap-[4px]
  gap-2             NOT gap-[8px]

General rule: before using an arbitrary value like [Xpx], check if a
named Tailwind utility exists for that value first. Only use arbitrary
values [Xpx] when no named token matches — for example custom values
like rounded-[22px] or text-[10px] that fall outside the default scale.
